WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.166 --> 00:00:02.235
It's a blockbuster holiday weekend.

00:00:02.235 --> 00:00:03.503
The highly anticipated

00:00:03.503 --> 00:00:05.472
movies, Oppenheimer and Barbie,

00:00:05.472 --> 00:00:07.307
are hitting theaters today.

00:00:07.307 --> 00:00:08.408
Our Sara Sidner sat down

00:00:08.408 --> 00:00:09.943
with two stars of the Barbie movie

00:00:09.943 --> 00:00:10.410
last month.

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:12.012
Before, I should note,

00:00:12.012 --> 00:00:13.413
the actors went on strike.

00:00:13.413 --> 00:00:14.948
And she joins us now.

00:00:14.948 --> 00:00:15.582
So, Sara,

00:00:15.582 --> 00:00:16.783
a lot of people don't know

00:00:16.783 --> 00:00:18.018
this about Margot Robbie,

00:00:18.018 --> 00:00:19.519
but she played a really critical role

00:00:19.519 --> 00:00:21.354
and even getting this movie

00:00:21.354 --> 00:00:23.456
to be created in the first place.

00:00:23.490 --> 00:00:25.258
What did they tell you?

00:00:25.258 --> 00:00:27.794
Some interesting things.

00:00:27.794 --> 00:00:28.561
I asked them,

00:00:28.561 --> 00:00:30.497
I said, look, when I was a little girl,

00:00:30.497 --> 00:00:31.598
I didn't play with Barbie.

00:00:31.598 --> 00:00:33.466
I was too busy jumping out of trees.

00:00:33.466 --> 00:00:34.267
And you were trying

00:00:34.267 --> 00:00:35.335
to be better than that?

00:00:35.335 --> 00:00:35.668
Well, no,

00:00:35.668 --> 00:00:36.603
I was just trying to be better

00:00:36.603 --> 00:00:38.204
than the boys all the time.

00:00:38.204 --> 00:00:39.506
Was very competitive.

00:00:39.506 --> 00:00:41.274
And Margot Robbie

00:00:41.274 --> 00:00:43.810
jumps up and says, me, too.

00:00:44.010 --> 00:00:45.478
And then America Ferrera says,

00:00:45.478 --> 00:00:47.247
I didn't play with Barbie either.

00:00:47.247 --> 00:00:49.549
And I was like, So what's with the movie?

00:00:49.549 --> 00:00:51.217
And both of them

00:00:53.486 --> 00:00:55.221
It's a great follow up.

00:00:55.221 --> 00:00:59.492
Both of them said, This movie has heart.

00:00:59.626 --> 00:01:00.126
Yeah.

00:01:00.126 --> 00:01:01.728
It will make you laugh,

00:01:01.728 --> 00:01:03.930
but it might also make you cry.

00:01:03.930 --> 00:01:05.298
It's deep.

00:01:05.298 --> 00:01:07.000
Barbie is deep.

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:08.201
That's what I learned.

00:01:08.201 --> 00:01:09.102
Take a listen.

00:01:10.904 --> 00:01:11.104
All right.

00:01:11.104 --> 00:01:11.871
I'm gonna start with you.

00:01:11.871 --> 00:01:12.372
Margot,

00:01:12.372 --> 00:01:15.442
everyone makes Barbie into who

00:01:15.475 --> 00:01:16.443
they think she is

00:01:16.443 --> 00:01:17.343
because she doesn't talk.

00:01:17.343 --> 00:01:18.411
She doesn't walk.

00:01:18.411 --> 00:01:20.013
So we use our imaginations.

00:01:20.013 --> 00:01:21.314
How did you decide

00:01:21.314 --> 00:01:23.550
who Barbie was going to be in this film?

00:01:23.817 --> 00:01:25.185
To be honest,

00:01:25.185 --> 00:01:28.555
Greta knew from the beginning,

00:01:28.555 --> 00:01:29.789
really, that she wanted Barbie

00:01:29.789 --> 00:01:32.158
to have the classic hero's journey.

00:01:32.792 --> 00:01:33.893
She actually used, like,

00:01:33.893 --> 00:01:35.829
Buddha's journey to enlightenment

00:01:35.829 --> 00:01:36.663
as a reference.

00:01:36.663 --> 00:01:38.198
And I was like, Okay, well,

00:01:38.198 --> 00:01:39.599
I didn't see that coming

00:01:39.599 --> 00:01:40.867
but now that you've said it, it

00:01:40.867 --> 00:01:42.001
does make perfect sense.

00:01:43.036 --> 00:01:43.870
And so

00:01:43.870 --> 00:01:44.637
suddenly, she did

00:01:44.637 --> 00:01:45.038
have, like,

00:01:45.038 --> 00:01:46.406
this framework of the narrative.

00:01:46.406 --> 00:01:47.040
And within that,

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:49.109
we can have all these conversations on

00:01:49.109 --> 00:01:50.343
so many different levels.

00:01:50.343 --> 00:01:52.412
And and what we wanted to do with

00:01:52.412 --> 00:01:54.481
those conversations is kind of honor

00:01:54.481 --> 00:01:55.448
the legacy

00:01:55.448 --> 00:01:58.451
that the 64 years of Barbie has created.

00:01:58.651 --> 00:01:59.385
You know,

00:01:59.385 --> 00:02:02.055
and also bring it into today's day.

00:02:02.055 --> 00:02:02.589
You know, have

00:02:02.589 --> 00:02:05.191
I have culturally relevant conversations.

00:02:05.758 --> 00:02:06.092
Okay.

00:02:06.092 --> 00:02:07.994
I do have to ask America

00:02:07.994 --> 00:02:09.362
how deliciously

00:02:09.362 --> 00:02:13.233
ironic is it that Ryan Gosling's age

00:02:13.433 --> 00:02:15.969
became the thing that people were

00:02:15.969 --> 00:02:17.370
talking about,

00:02:17.370 --> 00:02:20.039
not the woman, but the man for once.

00:02:20.874 --> 00:02:22.609
Oh yeah. It is ironic.

00:02:22.609 --> 00:02:23.877
Yeah, I just heard that.

00:02:23.877 --> 00:02:25.478
That's the thing.

00:02:25.712 --> 00:02:27.046
You know, that's the

00:02:27.046 --> 00:02:27.347
that's

00:02:27.347 --> 00:02:29.649
the fate of the cans in Barbie land, is

00:02:29.649 --> 00:02:31.851
they essentially have to suffer

00:02:31.851 --> 00:02:33.119
a lot of the

00:02:33.119 --> 00:02:35.421
the fate of women in the real world.

00:02:35.421 --> 00:02:37.957
And and, you know, it it

00:02:38.191 --> 00:02:40.860
it it kind of highlights its stupidity,

00:02:40.960 --> 00:02:41.494
really.

00:02:42.462 --> 00:02:43.296
But but

00:02:43.296 --> 00:02:44.831
it's you know, the

00:02:44.831 --> 00:02:47.300
movie turns a lot of things on its head.

00:02:47.500 --> 00:02:50.904
And and I in my opinion, tells us more

00:02:51.204 --> 00:02:53.239
about us as humans

00:02:54.207 --> 00:02:55.708
than than really,

00:02:55.708 --> 00:02:57.877
you know, a movie about dolls.

00:02:57.877 --> 00:02:58.545
And America

00:02:58.545 --> 00:02:59.812
you play one of the few characters

00:02:59.812 --> 00:03:02.582
who is not a doll, who is not a Barbie.

00:03:02.582 --> 00:03:03.483
In the movie.

00:03:03.483 --> 00:03:04.684
You're a Real-Life Person

00:03:04.684 --> 00:03:06.186
going through Real-Life Challenges

00:03:06.186 --> 00:03:07.787
as a working woman.

00:03:07.787 --> 00:03:10.490
What happens when you and Barbie meet

00:03:10.523 --> 00:03:11.658
finally?

00:03:11.658 --> 00:03:13.526
I don't want to spoil anything,

00:03:13.526 --> 00:03:14.861
but I don't spoil

00:03:14.861 --> 00:03:17.697
and give us a reason for

00:03:17.697 --> 00:03:18.364
the moment.

00:03:18.364 --> 00:03:20.567
That Gloria and Barbie connect.

00:03:20.567 --> 00:03:22.802
I just started, like, bawling, and.

00:03:22.802 --> 00:03:24.938
And it felt so

00:03:26.339 --> 00:03:29.142
beautiful that, you know, a grown woman

00:03:29.943 --> 00:03:32.312
could explore

00:03:32.312 --> 00:03:36.115
her imagination and her playfulness and

00:03:36.316 --> 00:03:38.685
and really be enthusing tastic

00:03:38.685 --> 00:03:41.387
